<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseHumanMakeableGun">
    <defName>Shahed_AntiDroneGun</defName>
    <label>anti-drone gun</label>
    <description>A handheld electronic warfare jammer: a big antenna housing up front, an electronics box with cooling fan, a carry handle and a battery pack. Aim it at an enemy drone (a recon drone circling over your colony, or an incoming FPV) to jam its control link: use "Jam drone" on the colonist holding it. The better the colonist's Shooting skill, the faster it works. A jammed drone usually crashes and leaves some salvage; sometimes it lands intact and you can keep it.\n\nIt is useless against anything that is not a drone.</description>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Shahed136/Weapons/AntiDroneGun</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>1.35</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Interact_Rifle</soundInteract>
    <weaponTags>
      <li>Shahed_AntiDroneJammer</li>
    </weaponTags>
    <statBases>
      <WorkToMake>30000</WorkToMake>
      <Mass>5</Mass>
      <AccuracyTouch>0.70</AccuracyTouch>
      <AccuracyShort>0.80</AccuracyShort>
      <AccuracyMedium>0.75</AccuracyMedium>
      <AccuracyLong>0.60</AccuracyLong>
      <RangedWeapon_Cooldown>1.7</RangedWeapon_Cooldown>
      <MarketValue>700</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <Steel>60</Steel>
      <ComponentIndustrial>5</ComponentIndustrial>
    </costList>
    <recipeMaker>
      <researchPrerequisite>Shahed_AntiDroneGuns</researchPrerequisite>
      <skillRequirements>
        <Crafting>6</Crafting>
      </skillRequirements>
      <displayPriority>500</displayPriority>
    </recipeMaker>
    <comps>
      <li Class="Shahed136Drones.CompProperties_DroneJammer">
        <range>54.9</range>
        <baseJamTicks>1200</baseJamTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>body</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>9</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
      </li>
    </tools>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
